{{Quote|12,000 credits. That's everything I owe. Xan, Nurchi, Brasso, Deema. Twelve should cover it.|Cassian Andor gives credits to Bix Caleen to pay off his debts|audio=Andor-Owed.flac|<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref>}}
'''Deema''' was one of the many people that the debtor [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] owed [[Currency|money]] to<ref name="Announcement" /> by [[5 BBY]].<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|107}}</ref> After fleeing his [[Andor household|home]] on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]] as a fugitive, Andor took part in a [[Aldhani heist|heist]] on the planet [[Aldhani]], receiving a cut of the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] payroll that was stolen. He then returned to Ferrix and gave twelve thousand [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] from his cut to the [[Caleen Salyard|store]] owner [[Bix Caleen]] to pay all off of his outstanding debts, including what he owed to the lenders Deema, [[Brasso]], [[Nurchi]], and [[Xanwan]].<ref name="Announcement" />

==Behind the scenes==
Deema was mentioned in "[[Announcement]]," the seventh episode of the [[Andor Season 1|first season]] of the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'',<ref name="Announcement" /> which aired on [[October 19]], [[2022]].<ref name="Release dates">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1557442379975573504|[[Star Wars]]|date=2022-8-10|quote=This is what revolution looks like. Watch #Andor, a Star Wars Original Series, streaming only on @DisneyPlus September 21.|archivedate=20220810191942}}</ref>

